WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.250
Kujo Hermes.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.050
Bring accountability to Hermes. Catch this checkout

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.610
overcharge before you trust the result.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.730
Define expected behavior with Spec. You control approval for

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.330
repository checks.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.970
Eval exposes the failure, giving your agent evidence to act on.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.730
Hermes corrects the calculation. The tests stay unchanged,

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.410
so the comparison holds.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.570
Now the same three checks pass.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:43.090
That’s accountability you can inspect: what ran, what passed, and

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.570
the evidence behind it.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.330
Discover Scout for repository insight, PackWrite for focused

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.370
context, and ShipCheck for release review.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.330
With Hermes, Kujo and Git installed, two commands connect

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.850
your workflow to Kujo.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:09.350
Kujo. Trust at the speed of AI. Install Kujo Hermes today.
